    R1["⚖️ THE PRICING LAW — WRITE IT INTO CLAUDE.md:<br/>ONE PRICE FEEDS BOTH COST LINES. Green (food cost) and gold (shop spend) share the<br/>SAME unit price, different multipliers.<br/>👉 SO 'ALWAYS TAKE THE MOST EXPENSIVE TO BE SAFE' IS FATAL. It inflates the GREEN<br/>number — and the green number is where Tinza claims COOKING BEATS BUYING.<br/>INFLATE IT AND YOU LOSE YOUR OWN ARGUMENT.<br/><br/>✅ PRICE WHAT A NORMAL PERSON PAYS AT A NORMAL SHOP. MID-MARKET. NOT CHEAPEST. NOT DEAREST.<br/>✅ TINZA PRICES ARE **CHECKERS** PRICES. Standard shelf. NEVER A SPECIAL.<br/>   Footer: 'Prices: Checkers, July 2026.' It PORTS: UK = Tesco. US = Kroger.<br/>✅ WHERE THE RETAIL SPREAD EXCEEDS ~2x → STORE A RANGE AND SAY SO ON THE CARD.<br/>   'Date syrup R95–R155 depending on brand.' THE MOST HONEST LINE IN THE APP."]
    R2["❌ THE '+X% UPLIFT' PLAN IS DEAD. The test was run twice and the two runs DISAGREE<br/>on which shop is dearer. The gap is an ARTEFACT OF THE BASKET, not a constant.<br/>👉 PICK ONE SHOP AND SAY WHICH. That is the whole fix."]
    R3["🛒 GROCIFY — grocifyapp.co.za. FREE, 7 SA retailers, real-time, barcode scan.<br/>✅ USE IT AS A TOOL. It is the Checkers walk, on the couch. AN EVENING, NOT A SATURDAY.<br/>✅ PARTNERSHIP — POST-LAUNCH. Their Smart Cart WANTS a list. Tinza PRODUCES one.<br/>⛔ NEVER A LIVE DEPENDENCY. No API · brand-new startup · and ☠️ OFFLINE MODE IS A<br/>LOCKED TINZA FEATURE. A PWA that works without signal CANNOT fetch live prices.<br/>PRICE_DB STAYS A STATIC, DATED, HUMAN-SIGNED SNAPSHOT. THAT IS THE HONESTY."]
    R4["🏗️ PRICE STUDIO — BUILD IT (a day; copy Photo Studio, which already works).<br/>Ranks every key by IMPACT × STALENESS × CONFIDENCE. Prints a WORKLIST.<br/>👉 FLOUR IS IN ~400 DISHES. DATE SYRUP IS IN 3. NOT THE SAME JOB.<br/>📊 GATE ON THIS COUNT (read-only, queue it): how many DISTINCT PRICE_DB keys?<br/>Top 100 by usage? What % of ALL costed lines do the top 100 cover?<br/>👉 IF THE TOP 100 COVERS 90%+, the price problem is 100 items and an afternoon at<br/>Checkers, QUARTERLY — not a scraping project. THAT NUMBER DECIDES EVERYTHING.<br/>🌱 THE FALLBACK CENSUS IS ITS FIRST HALF. Build that and Price Studio is half done."]
    R1 --> R2 --> R3 --> R4
  end

  subgraph DIETLOCK["🥬 DIETARY — LOCKED 12 JUL (supersedes 27 Jun AND the old Free/Pro line)"]
    D1["💰 V IS PRO. FREE GETS ZERO FILTERING.<br/>👉 KILLS the old 'Free = 1 dietary restriction' line. DEAD.<br/>🎁 BADGE FREE · FILTER PRO. The V/VE badge renders on EVERY card for EVERYONE —<br/>IT IS THE PITCH. The filter bar is PRO.<br/>WHY: a Free vegan who sees no V anywhere doesn't hit a paywall — SHE LEAVES.<br/>A BLANK IS A BUG. A TEASER IS A PITCH. THE LOCK IS THE SALESMAN.<br/>ONBOARDING: 👉 FREE ASKS. PRO APPLIES."]
    D2["📋 V + VE ONLY FOR v1. The 12-tag taxonomy is a design doc with ZERO DATA behind it.<br/>🚩 FOURTH STATE REQUIRED: diet:'unknown'. Untagged must NEVER default and NEVER<br/>appear in the VE filter. FAIL LOUD. An untagged dish quietly counting as 'vegan'<br/>is the one that ends you.<br/>NOTHING HIDES ITSELF. Hard-hide killed by THE VEGAN MOM WHO COOKS FOR HER<br/>NON-VEGAN FAMILY. Auto-apply parked → post-launch Settings checkbox."]
    D3["🏗️ SHELVES ARE QUERIES, NOT LISTS. Tag ONCE. A shelf = a QUERY on the diet field.<br/>ONE FIELD → THREE VIEWS: badge · filter · shelf.<br/>Hand-built V/VE shelves RULED AGAINST: two sources of truth, and it builds a<br/>ghetto (vegan food ONLY in the vegan room)."]
    D4["⚠️ TAGS DERIVED IN NODE FROM INGREDIENT LISTS. NEVER BY HAND.<br/>Last audit: CAESAR SALAD tagged vegetarian WITH ANCHOVIES IN IT.<br/>🔍 HIDDEN-ANIMAL DICTIONARY — REQUIRED: worcestershire (anchovy) · fish sauce ·<br/>oyster sauce · shrimp paste · dashi/bonito · chicken stock · gelatine · lard/suet.<br/>Not vegan: honey · butter · ghee · milk powder.<br/>🧀 PARMESAN/PECORINO → diet:'veg' + NEW FIELD dietNote (rennet is unknowable).<br/>⛔ dietNote IS FOR THE GENUINELY UNKNOWABLE ONLY. NOT AN ESCAPE HATCH.<br/>☪️ HALAAL + KOSHER: separate laws, never swap-guided. We can say NO PORK · NO<br/>ALCOHOL. We CANNOT say CERTIFIED HALAAL. Never claim it."]
    D1 --> D2 --> D3 --> D4
  end

  subgraph TRUTH["💣 THE COSTING TRUTH — THE MATHS. STILL NOT STARTED."]
    T1["MF29 — COUNT-ITEM OVER-BILLING. Math.ceil in the FOOD-COST path.<br/>mealsCostPP (core:3338) · lineCook (core:2765) · wkCostRecipe (worldkitchen:501)<br/>ceil is CORRECT for shopping (can't buy half an egg) = GOLD<br/>ceil is CATASTROPHIC for food cost (a slice holds 0.4 egg) = GREEN<br/>319 of 440 lines are in BAKES → ~2.5x overstated → A HOME CAKE MAY 'COST' MORE<br/>THAN A BOUGHT ONE. THAT IS THE PRODUCT'S CORE CLAIM, INVERTED.<br/>✅ REFERENCE IMPL EXISTS: costRecipe does it right. PROPAGATE IT. Copying, not inventing."]
    T2["MF33 — THE SILENT ONE. hcLineCost (health:597) + ttLineCost (tinyTummies:6)<br/>RETURN NULL FOR COUNT ITEMS → Health &amp; Tiny Tummies DON'T COST EGGS AT ALL.<br/>The app OVER-bills eggs in FMF/Braai/WK and UNDER-bills them in Health/Kiddies.<br/>✅ FIX PATTERN ALREADY ON SCREEN: 'Based on 8/9 ingredients priced.'<br/>MAKE IT UNIVERSAL — IT IS THE HONESTY FEATURE, NOT AN ERROR MESSAGE."]
    T3["🩸 health.js IS STILL THE MOST BROKEN FILE IN TINZA.<br/>It carried the only surviving gate leak, MF28, MF33, MF34 — and it is<br/>WHERE THE DIETARY USERS LIVE. Every road leads back here."]
    T1 --> T2 --> T3
  end

  subgraph COLOUR["🎨 MF31 + MF32 — COLOUR LAW (now trivial)"]
    P1["LAW: green = food cost · gold = shop spend · NEVER MIX. Honoured in 1 room of 12.<br/>BRAAI → shop-gold on a FOOD figure ❌ · WK → orange, a THIRD colour ❌<br/>…and a variable literally NAMED 'green' that RESOLVES TO ORANGE (worldkitchen:570)<br/>✅ GOLD STANDARD: shoppingView. Copy it.<br/>🎁 NOW TRIVIAL: colour lives in costLine(). ONE function. Was ten boxes.<br/>MF32 — ingredient 'total' WEIGHTS render in shop-spend gold. A weight is not money."]
  end

