  subgraph LAW["⚖️ THE LAW"]
    W1["1. node --check PROVES NOTHING. It passed on a ZERO-BYTE spice.js.<br/><br/>2. A REPORT IS NOT PROOF. A PASSING TEST IS A REPORT TOO.<br/>PROVE IT PER-SECTION. 5 of 12 is not proof. A bad room hides inside a good aggregate.<br/><br/>3. SILENT WRONG IS WORSE THAN LOUD MISSING.<br/><br/>4. A NARROW QUESTION GETS A NARROW ANSWER — AND IT WILL BE TRUE.<br/>ASK 'WHAT IS NOT GUARDED?' — NEVER 'is X guarded?'<br/><br/>5. LOCALHOST IS NOT LIVE. COMMITTED IS NOT PUSHED. PUSHED IS NOT DEPLOYED.<br/><br/>6. DON'T PATCH N SITES. BUILD THE ONE THING THEY SHOULD ALL CALL.<br/><br/>7. A BLANK IS A BUG. A TEASER IS A PITCH. THE LOCK IS THE SALESMAN.<br/><br/>8. 'SHIP IT' IS NOT 'PUSH IT'. Say which one you mean.<br/><br/>9. A CONTEXT-DEPENDENT RULE MUST NEVER BE ENCODED AS A CONTEXT-FREE ALIAS.<br/>The Meat Cut Guide is a METHOD → CUT rule. An alias does not know the method.<br/>Flatten one into the other and A GOOD RULE BECOMES A SILENT LIE. (lamb → lamb neck.)<br/><br/>10. THE BUG WAS IN THE DATA, NOT THE CODE. THREE TIMES IN ONE DAY.<br/>THE RESOLVER WAS NEVER LYING. IT WAS FAITHFULLY READING LIES WE WROTE OURSELVES.<br/>Guards are the NET. The DATA is the FIX.<br/><br/>11. NO MODEL AUTHORS A PRICE. EVER. 3 of 4 guesses were out by 2.5x–4x.<br/>A PRICE WITH NO PROVENANCE IS A RUMOUR. src + when + conf, or it doesn't ship.<br/><br/>12. FAIL-LOUD IS THE NET. PRICED-CORRECTLY IS THE GOAL.<br/>Don't ship 7 loud blanks when the answer was already sitting in the database.<br/><br/>13. 🆕 A GUARD THAT NULLS A CORRECT ANSWER IS A BUG, NOT A SAFETY FEATURE.<br/>L3 nulled 'coconut oil for frying'. That is a correct key. L3 died on its own evidence.<br/><br/>14. 🆕 DRY-RUN BEFORE SHIP. Code proposed L3, dry-ran it, and killed its own design.<br/>EVERY GUARD GETS ITS FALSE-POSITIVE LIST BEFORE IT IS BUILT. THAT IS THE STANDARD NOW.<br/><br/>15. 🆕 A RULING THAT LIVES ONLY IN THE CHAT IS NOT A RULING.<br/>Code sat blocked on four questions Tina had ALREADY ANSWERED. IT GOES IN THE BRIEF.<br/><br/>16. 🆕 A COOK'S RULE IS NOT A SHOPPER'S RULE.<br/>The Meat Cut Guide says 'stewing lamb = shoulder or neck'. TRUE IN THE KITCHEN.<br/>USELESS AT THE TILL. YOU CANNOT BUY 'SHOULDER OR NECK' — you buy a PACK.<br/>👉 THE INGREDIENT STANDARD IS THE PRICING STANDARD: THE NAME IS WHAT YOU BUY.<br/>If a key is not something a human can put in a trolley, IT IS NOT A KEY.<br/><br/>17. 🆕 CONTEXT-FLATTENING HAPPENS AT THE KEY LEVEL TOO, NOT JUST THE ALIAS LEVEL.<br/>'lamb knuckle / potjiekos' as one key merges a CUT with a MIX.<br/>'lamb stew / lamb mince' merges GROUND meat with CUBED BONE-IN.<br/>A merged key AVERAGES A REAL DIFFERENCE INTO A FAKE ONE. Same disease. New coat.<br/><br/>18. 🆕 RECONCILE, DO NOT ADD. A new key beside an old key for the SAME PRODUCT<br/>gives you TWO PRICES AND A COIN TOSS. Print the current list. Sign one number. Then write.<br/><br/>19. 🆕 LAW 11 DOES NOT CARE WHO WROTE THE NUMBER DOWN.<br/>'No model authors a price' was aimed at Code. Then lamb mince came in at R98 —<br/>2.2x under, and almost certainly BEEF MINCE wearing a lamb label. TINA'S OWN NOTE.<br/>👉 A PRICE WITH NO PROVENANCE IS A RUMOUR. MODEL OR HUMAN. NO EXCEPTIONS.<br/>A number that sits in the notes long enough STARTS TO LOOK LIKE A FACT.<br/>src + when + conf, or it doesn't ship. conf:'online' is not conf:'shelf'."]
  end

